WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.063
The workbook's third chapter keeps
the workflows as reviewed files.

2
00:00:04.063 --> 00:00:06.774
Its lint passes the program's six files.

3
00:00:06.774 --> 00:00:11.774
Against three broken copies, it catches
an offset outside Microsoft's range,

4
00:00:11.774 --> 00:00:15.742
too many workflows for the
budget, a missing execution limit,

5
00:00:15.742 --> 00:00:18.043
a joiner that adds groups directly,

6
00:00:18.043 --> 00:00:22.725
delete and disable in the same workflow,
and a pass that lasts three days.

7
00:00:22.725 --> 00:00:26.575
The plan step refuses to run
if any file has a finding.

8
00:00:26.575 --> 00:00:29.650
Then it compares each file
with the tenant's export.

9
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:34.256
A missing workflow becomes a create,
and a changed one becomes a new version,

10
00:00:34.256 --> 00:00:37.525
because workflows are
versioned, not edited in place.

11
00:00:37.525 --> 00:00:40.300
It reads with one permission
and sends nothing.

12
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:44.837
Execution limits aren't in the
API, so record them in the file.

13
00:00:44.837 --> 00:00:49.151
Last, readiness checks each hire
for an enabled, licensed account,

14
00:00:49.151 --> 00:00:52.587
the onboarding package, and
a completed pre-hire run.

15
00:00:52.587 --> 00:00:54.987
One of four fictional hires is ready.

16
00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:57.410
Run it on an export from
the start of the day.
